{"id":"crossbar","path":"docs/modules/crossbar/eli5.md","title":"Module 2: Crossbar - Compute-in-Memory","category":"Learning","sha256":"f93cca6de07afe4ca69feb254bd14c6beb585dcaca904b3672fc712cf441e3b7","rights":"MIT","attribution":"FeCIM Lattice Tools contributors (repository-authored Markdown; publisher assets excluded)","bytes":8771,"terms":["1T1R","ADC","DAC","FeCIM","Hysteresis Loop","IR Drop","MVM","Sneak Path","TIA"],"headings":[{"text":"Module 2: Crossbar - Compute-in-Memory","level":1,"anchor":"module-2-crossbar---compute-in-memory"},{"text":"Evidence Status (Demonstrated vs Modeled vs Aspirational)","level":2,"anchor":"evidence-status-demonstrated-vs-modeled-vs-aspirational"},{"text":"The Magic: Ohm's Law is Multiplication","level":2,"anchor":"the-magic-ohms-law-is-multiplication"},{"text":"What is a Crossbar?","level":2,"anchor":"what-is-a-crossbar"},{"text":"How It Computes (Step by Step)","level":2,"anchor":"how-it-computes-step-by-step"},{"text":"Why This is Powerful","level":2,"anchor":"why-this-is-powerful"},{"text":"Traditional CPU","level":3,"anchor":"traditional-cpu"},{"text":"Crossbar","level":3,"anchor":"crossbar"},{"text":"The Three Real-World Problems","level":2,"anchor":"the-three-real-world-problems"},{"text":"1. IR Drop (Voltage Gets Weak)","level":3,"anchor":"1-ir-drop-voltage-gets-weak"},{"text":"2. Sneak Paths (Current Takes Shortcuts)","level":3,"anchor":"2-sneak-paths-current-takes-shortcuts"},{"text":"3. Variation (Each Cell is Slightly Different)","level":3,"anchor":"3-variation-each-cell-is-slightly-different"},{"text":"The Demo: Three Views","level":2,"anchor":"the-demo-three-views"},{"text":"View 1: Conductance Map","level":3,"anchor":"view-1-conductance-map"},{"text":"View 2: IR Drop Analysis","level":3,"anchor":"view-2-ir-drop-analysis"},{"text":"View 3: Sneak Path Visualization","level":3,"anchor":"view-3-sneak-path-visualization"},{"text":"Multi-Level Baseline (30 States)","level":2,"anchor":"multi-level-baseline-30-states"},{"text":"Key Parameters for Design","level":2,"anchor":"key-parameters-for-design"},{"text":"How to Run Module 2","level":2,"anchor":"how-to-run-module-2"},{"text":"The Full Inference Path","level":2,"anchor":"the-full-inference-path"},{"text":"Key Takeaways","level":2,"anchor":"key-takeaways"},{"text":"Real Crossbars in Practice","level":2,"anchor":"real-crossbars-in-practice"},{"text":"Next Steps","level":2,"anchor":"next-steps"}],"nodes":[{"kind":"heading","level":1,"anchor":"module-2-crossbar---compute-in-memory","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Module 2: Crossbar - Compute-in-Memory"}]},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"evidence-status-demonstrated-vs-modeled-vs-aspirational","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Evidence Status (Demonstrated vs Modeled vs Aspirational)"}]},{"kind":"list","children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Demonstrated:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" MVM operation, quantization to 30 levels, heatmap visualization are implemented in this repo and verifiable from source/tests."}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Modeled:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" IR drop, sneak paths, drift, device variation are simulator models unless explicitly tied to cited measured data."}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aspirational:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Full peripheral integration and GPU acceleration are roadmap intent and must not be reported as demonstrated results."}]}]}]},{"kind":"quote","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explain Like I'm 5:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Physics does multiplication for free when you use a crossbar array"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"the-magic-ohms-law-is-multiplication","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Magic: Ohm's Law is Multiplication"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Discovered in 1827, Ohm's Law is simple:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Current = Voltage × Conductance\n   I    =    V    ×      G\n\nThis is just... multiplication! Physics does it for free!\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The insight:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" If we:"}]},{"kind":"list","ordered":true,"children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Store weights as conductance (G)"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Send inputs as voltage (V)"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The current that flows out (I) IS the result"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"what-is-a-crossbar","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What is a Crossbar?"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's a grid of wires with a memory cell at each intersection:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"        Columns (send voltages in)\n           V₀    V₁    V₂    V₃\n           │     │     │     │\nRow 0  ────●─────●─────●─────●────→ I₀ (current out)\n           │     │     │     │\nRow 1  ────●─────●─────●─────●────→ I₁\n           │     │     │     │\nRow 2  ────●─────●─────●─────●────→ I₂\n           │     │     │     │\nRow 3  ────●─────●─────●─────●────→ I₃\n\n● = one memory cell (conductance = weight)\n"},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"how-it-computes-step-by-step","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How It Computes (Step by Step)"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Step 1: Store weights in cells\n        ┌─────────────┐\n        │ G₀₀ G₀₁ G₀₂ │ Row 0\n        │ G₁₀ G₁₁ G₁₂ │ Row 1\n        │ G₂₀ G₂₁ G₂₂ │ Row 2\n        └─────────────┘\n\nStep 2: Apply input voltages to columns\n        V₀ = 0.3V\n        V₁ = 0.5V\n        V₂ = 0.2V\n\nStep 3: Current flows (multiplication happens!)\n        Row 0 output = G₀₀×V₀ + G₀₁×V₁ + G₀₂×V₂\n                     = 0.2×0.3 + 0.8×0.5 + 0.4×0.2\n                     = 0.06 + 0.40 + 0.08 = 0.54A\n\nStep 4: All rows compute in PARALLEL!\n        Row 0: 0.54A\n        Row 1: 0.42A\n        Row 2: 0.61A\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is matrix-vector multiplication!"}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"why-this-is-powerful","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Why This is Powerful"}]},{"kind":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"traditional-cpu","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Traditional CPU"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"To multiply a 1000×1000 matrix by a vector:\n- 1 million multiplications\n- Each one: fetch → multiply → store\n- Sequential: one at a time\n- Time: millions of clock cycles\n- Energy: billions of transistor switches\n"},{"kind":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"crossbar","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Crossbar"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"To multiply a 1000×1000 matrix by a vector:\n- 1 million multiplications\n- All happen AT THE SAME TIME\n- Parallel: all in one analog operation\n- Time: ~nanoseconds\n- Energy: physics doing the work\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Same result. 1000× faster. 1000× less energy (projected; see honesty audit for caveats)."}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"the-three-real-world-problems","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Three Real-World Problems"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Real crossbars aren't perfect. Three things go wrong:"}]},{"kind":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"1-ir-drop-voltage-gets-weak","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1. IR Drop (Voltage Gets Weak)"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Sent voltage: 1.0V ───→ 0.95V ───→ 0.90V ───→ 0.85V\n                          ↓ gets weaker as it travels!\n\nWhy? Wires have resistance (like friction)\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Impact:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Inputs at the end of a long wire are weaker, so outputs are wrong."}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Interleaving decoders, distributed drivers, or shorter wires."}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"2-sneak-paths-current-takes-shortcuts","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2. Sneak Paths (Current Takes Shortcuts)"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Goal: Current through only the target cell (●)\n      →→→●→→→\n\nReality: Current is lazy and takes ALL paths!\n        →→→●→→→\n        ↓   ↑\n       →→→●→→→ (snuck through unselected cells!)\n\nCurrent leaks through unwanted cells!\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Impact:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" The current you measure isn't just from the target cell."}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Selector devices (like diodes) at each cell to block backflow."}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"3-variation-each-cell-is-slightly-different","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3. Variation (Each Cell is Slightly Different)"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Set two cells to \"0.5 conductance\":\nCell A: 0.48 (slightly less conductive)\nCell B: 0.52 (slightly more conductive)\n\nWhy? Fabrication isn't perfect (atoms arrange differently)\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Impact:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" You get ±2-5% errors per cell, which add up."}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Error correction, redundancy, or careful characterization."}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"the-demo-three-views","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Demo: Three Views"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Module 2 shows you three tabbed views:"}]},{"kind":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"view-1-conductance-map","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"View 1: Conductance Map"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n│ ░░░ ░░░ ███ ░░░                │\n│ ░░░ ██░ ░░░ ░░░                │\n│ ███ ░░░ ░░░ ░░░                │\n│ ░░░ ░░░ ░░░ ██░                │\n└─────────────────────────────────┘\n\nDark = high conductance (strong weight)\nLight = low conductance (weak weight)\n\nClick a cell to select it and see details.\n"},{"kind":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"view-2-ir-drop-analysis","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"View 2: IR Drop Analysis"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Shows voltage loss along each row/column.\nHighlights problem areas that need fixing.\n"},{"kind":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"view-3-sneak-path-visualization","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"View 3: Sneak Path Visualization"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Shows unwanted current leakage.\nDemonstrates why selector devices matter.\n"},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"multi-level-baseline-30-states","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Multi-Level Baseline (30 States)"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Instead of binary (0 or 1), we store multiple levels:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Conductance Levels (30-level demo baseline):\n\n0.00 ├─ Level 0  (lowest)\n0.03 ├─ Level 1\n0.07 ├─ Level 2\n⋮    ├─ ⋮\n0.50 ├─ Level 15  (middle)\n⋮    ├─ ⋮\n0.93 ├─ Level 29\n1.00 ├─ Level 30  (maximum)\n\nMore levels = more precision per cell!\n"},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"key-parameters-for-design","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Key Parameters for Design"}]},{"kind":"table","children":[{"kind":"table-head","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Parameter"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Symbol"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Typical"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Trade-off"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Array Size"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M×N"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"128×128"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Larger = more compute, but more IR drop"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Max Voltage"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"V_"},{"kind":"text","text":"max"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1.0V"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Higher = stronger computation, but more power"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Min Conductance"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G_"},{"kind":"text","text":"min"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0.001 S"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lower = smaller leakage, but harder to control"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Wire Resistance"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R_"},{"kind":"text","text":"wire"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0.1 Ω"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lower = less IR drop, but need better wires"}]}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"how-to-run-module-2","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How to Run Module 2"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"go build -o fecim-lattice-tools ./cmd/fecim-lattice-tools\n./fecim-lattice-tools crossbar\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Try this:"}]}]},{"kind":"list","ordered":true,"children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Click a cell in the conductance map"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Watch the IR drop and sneak paths change"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Adjust the array size slider"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"See how problems get worse with larger arrays"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Think about solutions"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"the-full-inference-path","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Full Inference Path"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"From input to output:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Digital Input (bits)\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────┐\n│   DAC   │ ← Digital-to-Analog Converter\n│         │   (turns bits into voltages)\n└────┬────┘\n     │ Analog voltages\n     ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│   CROSSBAR ARRAY             │  ← Physics does\n│   (matrix-vector multiply)   │     multiplication!\n└────┬───────────────────────────┘\n     │ Analog currents\n     ▼\n┌─────────┐\n│   TIA   │ ← Transimpedance Amplifier\n│         │   (current to voltage)\n└────┬────┘\n     │ Small voltage\n     ▼\n┌─────────┐\n│   ADC   │ ← Analog-to-Digital Converter\n│         │   (voltages back to bits)\n└────┬────┘\n     │\n     ▼\nDigital Output (bits)\n"},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"key-takeaways","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Key Takeaways"}]},{"kind":"table","children":[{"kind":"table-head","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Concept"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Remember This"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ohm's Law"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I = V × G (physics does multiplication)"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Crossbar"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Grid where all multiplications happen at once"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MVM"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Matrix-Vector Multiplication (core of AI)"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"IR Drop"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Voltage weakens traveling along wires"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sneak Paths"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Current leaks through unselected cells"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Variation"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each cell is slightly different"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"30 Levels"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Demo baseline for analog weight precision"}]}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"real-crossbars-in-practice","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Real Crossbars in Practice"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Modern ReRAM, MRAM, and PCM crossbars solve these problems with:"}]},{"kind":"list","children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Selector devices (1T1R, 1D1R) to block sneak paths"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Careful circuit design to minimize IR drop"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Statistical testing to characterize variation"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Error correction codes to handle noise"}]}]}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ferroelectric CIM uses the same techniques"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"next-steps","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next Steps"}]},{"kind":"list","children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Want to see it recognize digits?"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Go to "},{"kind":"link","url":"doc:mnist","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Module 3: MNIST"}]}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Want to learn about the circuits?"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Go to "},{"kind":"link","url":"doc:circuits","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Module 4: Circuits"}]}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Back to Module 1?"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" See "},{"kind":"link","url":"doc:hysteresis","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Module 1: Hysteresis"}]}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Back to overview?"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" See "},{"kind":"link","url":"doc:curriculum","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ELI5 Overview"}]}]}]}]}]}
